#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:12
msgid ""
"This implementation chunk contains 30 files under "
"`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/`: the Modelo 100 draft parser, censal-"
"certificate refusal boundary, filed-declaration parser, structured "
"e-invoice readers, and financial provider boundary plus mapped-tabular "
"fallback. The manifest measures 47,391 proxy tokens. I read every "
"assigned file in full, splitting the two long parsers into bounded line "
"ranges. This report is static analysis of the on-disk snapshot; it does "
"not run parsers or establish that external services, registries, or "
"downstream application flows work at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:14
msgid "Product capabilities and actors"
msgstr "Capacidades del producto y actores"

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:16
msgid ""
"For a taxpayer or operator importing a Renta document, `parse_borrador` "
"reads an AEAT Modelo 100 borrador, preview simulation, or filed "
"declaration into an observation of printed casilla values. It detects "
"`VISTA PREVIA` first, then a CSV stamp, then `BORRADOR`; callers can "
"override the kind and the year, which otherwise defaults to 2025. A per-"
"year table registers the same observed-row extractor for 2021–2025. The "
"detector and public entry point are in borrador/_detect.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/borrador/_detect.py`) and "
"borrador/parser.py (`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/borrador/parser.py`); "
"the registration table is in borrador/_extractors/selection.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/borrador/_extractors/selection.py`). Rows "
"follow a four-digit casilla plus amount grammar; first duplicates are "
"retained and later duplicates or unparseable amounts become warnings. An "
"optional caller-projected extraction profile filters values and can "
"enforce a minimum coverage fraction. The adapter itself does not resolve "
"a tax registry or claim the extracted set is complete. The extractor "
"records every value at page 1, with no bounding box and confidence 1.0, "
"even though it concatenates page text before matching; these fields "
"should not be read as spatially verified measurements "
"(modelo_100_summary_v2025.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/borrador/_extractors/modelo_100_summary_v2025.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:18
msgid ""
"For filed declarations, path and in-memory byte entry points converge on "
"a registry-profile-driven flow. The parser detects or accepts a template "
"coordinate, resolves a period, loads or accepts a `RegistrySnapshot`, "
"selects its `declaracion_pdf` extraction profile, validates the tax "
"identifier, and extracts profile targets. The returned observation "
"contains the parsed values, template and registry references, source "
"digest, and provisional-layout flag. The bytes route is explicitly "
"intended for decrypted live-read PDFs and keeps their content in memory "
"(declaracion/parser.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/declaracion/parser.py`), "
"declaracion/parser.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/declaracion/parser.py`)). Extraction "
"supports numeric casilla, named-label, and bounding-box strategies. "
"Bounding-box extraction uses page words and spatial limits; named-label "
"amounts may also use word positions to separate overprinted form numbers."
" Malformed and ambiguous targets always fail; missing targets fail only "
"when resulting coverage falls below the registry threshold "
"(declaracion/parser.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/declaracion/parser.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:20
msgid ""
"The censal certificate adapter currently has no extraction capability. It"
" checks the PDF magic header, then refuses both non-PDF and PDF input "
"with separate translated error keys. Its module states that no real "
"specimen has been observed, so it will not guess a layout "
"(censo/parser.py (`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/censo/parser.py`)). This "
"is an explicit unsupported state, not a partially implemented successful "
"parser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:22
msgid ""
"For structured invoices, `parse_einvoice_document` accepts standalone "
"CII, UBL, or Facturae XML and PDF/A-3-style containers with embedded XML."
" It reads seller and buyer roles, identifiers, names, addresses, invoice "
"identifiers and dates, totals, tax bands, and line items into one syntax-"
"independent DTO, then `translate_parsed_einvoice` copies that DTO into "
"application-owned ledger contracts (einvoice/parsers.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/einvoice/parsers.py`), "
"einvoice/application_translation.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/einvoice/application_translation.py`)). "
"The code takes tax IDs from explicitly VAT-tagged values when possible "
"and otherwise uses a broad two-letter-prefix-plus-digit shape heuristic; "
"it does not checksum-validate the e-invoice party ID in this chunk "
"(einvoice/parsers.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/einvoice/parsers.py`)). Tax-category codes"
" are looked up through the domain IVA category catalogue; the syntax "
"adapters otherwise carry many values as stated rather than deciding their"
" legal effect. Shape probing also identifies SII and VERI*FACTU payload "
"families, but this invoice parser’s dispatch table only implements CII, "
"UBL, and Facturae. Identification of those other shapes is not the same "
"as parsing them here (einvoice/shape.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/einvoice/shape.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:24
msgid ""
"The financial boundary turns provider-specific rows and exceptions into "
"application ledger contracts. It routes `auto`/`n26` through content "
"detection and explicit CSV, OFX/QFX, XLSX/Excel, and N26 PDF IDs to "
"concrete providers. The provider files for those formats are outside this"
" chunk, so their parsing behavior cannot be confirmed here "
"(financial/ledger_import.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/financial/ledger_import.py`)). The mapped-"
"tabular provider is a fallback lane for otherwise unclaimed delimited "
"tables. It maps columns once, requires date and amount roles, parses "
"every row independently, imports usable rows, and reports unmapped "
"columns, duplicate role assignments, and rejected rows. A valid source "
"needs at least one parseable row (providers/_mapped_tabular.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/financial/providers/_mapped_tabular.py`), "
"providers/_mapped_tabular.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/financial/providers/_mapped_tabular.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:26
msgid "How it works"
msgstr "Cómo funciona"

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:28
msgid ""
"The two Modelo 100 entry points have different I/O profiles: the path "
"version detects the artefact and then the extractor reads the PDF again, "
"while the byte version extracts page text once and passes it through "
"detection and extraction. Both hash the original bytes and derive a "
"privacy-preserving source reference. Required NIF and exercise-year "
"header fields must match; a declaration must also carry an AEAT CSV. "
"Profile coverage is computed from matched target casillas, and a below-"
"minimum result raises a typed `BorradorParseError` with missing IDs and "
"coverage. One contract discrepancy is visible: "
"`BorradorParseMode.OBSERVED` is documented as returning observed rows "
"without coverage enforcement, but passing `extraction_profile` in that "
"mode still sends the profile to the extractor, which filters rows and "
"enforces its minimum. The public parser only checks the mode when "
"registry-profile mode lacks a profile (borrador/parser.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/borrador/parser.py`), "
"modelo_100_summary_v2025.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/borrador/_extractors/modelo_100_summary_v2025.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:30
msgid ""
"Declaration detection reads the first two pages’ first 4,000 characters "
"plus up to 2,000 characters from the last page for model, year, and an "
"optional `Orden HAC` revision. If those fields are unavailable, explicit "
"model and year are required; supplying all three template coordinates "
"skips detection. A provided snapshot is checked against the template only"
" for `modelo.id`; the local check does not compare its revision, filing "
"year, or period with the resolved template and period, yet the snapshot "
"profile and its own reference are used in the returned observation "
"(declaracion/parser.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/declaracion/parser.py`), "
"declaracion/parser.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/declaracion/parser.py`)). This is a "
"concrete compatibility gap for callers that can pass a snapshot unrelated"
" to the other coordinates. When no snapshot is passed, an indexed "
"authority operation selects an applicability-grade snapshot and uses the "
"receipt presentation date to disambiguate a revision where needed "
"(declaracion/parser.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/declaracion/parser.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:32
msgid ""
"For declaration extraction, the path backend tries a pypdfium2 fast path,"
" accepts it only when declaration canaries match, and falls back to "
"pdfplumber. Path results are cached with size, modification time, and "
"content digest as the cache key; byte results are cached by digest in a "
"bounded in-memory dictionary. Word-position extraction is lazy and "
"prefers supplied bytes over a disk path. PDFium pages and text pages are "
"closed in `finally` blocks. The extraction failures are structured as "
"missing, malformed, ambiguous, and coverage data. However, missing "
"targets that remain within the profile’s minimum coverage are returned "
"without an advisory: the observation hard-codes `warnings=()` and does "
"not expose successful coverage. That makes an allowed partial extraction "
"difficult for downstream users to distinguish from a complete one "
"(declaracion/parser.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/declaracion/parser.py`), "
"declaracion/parser.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/declaracion/parser.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:34
msgid ""
"The e-invoice shape probe uses document bytes and recognized XML root or "
"AEAT payload names rather than caller MIME type or file suffix. PDF "
"embedded-file names only rank candidate order; content shape determines "
"whether the payload is treated as an invoice. XML is parsed through "
"`defusedxml` with a 32 MiB payload cap and a 100-level nesting limit. The"
" depth check is iterative but runs after XML construction, so the byte "
"cap is the earlier resource bound (einvoice/shape.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/einvoice/shape.py`), einvoice/xml.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/einvoice/xml.py`)). A PDF containing "
"multiple readable invoice attachments yields the first accepted candidate"
" in ranked order; this chunk does not report ambiguity or combine "
"invoices. Numeric XML values use machine-text decimal coercion. Missing "
"or unparseable values can remain `None` in the mutable DTO; mandatory-"
"field and arithmetic acceptance policy must be resolved downstream. The "
"parser also captures text-node-only `record_text` with separators to "
"avoid treating markup names or assembled adjacent values as evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:36
msgid ""
"Mapped tabular input is normalized by `core.tabular`, passed as a "
"`NormalizedTable` to the application column-role resolver, projected into"
" role/value pairs, then converted into raw transactions. Date parsing is "
"day-first; amount parsing follows the detected decimal separator; "
"currency codes are normalized and missing currency uses the provider "
"default. Transaction IDs use a source-provided ID when available, "
"otherwise a deterministic digest-and-row-derived ID. Unmapped columns and"
" ambiguous role claims are reported; the first duplicated role wins. Row "
"failures are skipped during ingest, while validation dry-runs all rows "
"and returns the aggregate diagnostics (providers/_mapped_tabular.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/financial/providers/_mapped_tabular.py`), "
"providers/_mapped_tabular.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/financial/providers/_mapped_tabular.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:38
msgid "Knowledge and data"
msgstr "Conocimiento y datos"

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:40
msgid ""
"Modelo 100 values are observations copied from PDF text; coverage "
"profiles are supplied by the caller, so the parser does not itself "
"establish registry authority. Declaration parsing uses validated registry"
" snapshots and extraction profiles, and stamps a `RegistrySnapshotRef` so"
" downstream logic can re-resolve the interpretation coordinate. The "
"declaration snapshot compatibility check described above is narrower than"
" the coordinate stamped into the observation. E-invoice tax category "
"meaning comes from the IVA category catalogue, while country codes remain"
" in each format’s stated code system (Facturae alpha-3 versus CII/UBL "
"alpha-2); no country-code conversion is done here. Financial tabular row "
"values become `RawTransaction` records with source provenance; mapped-"
"tabular exports declare `synthetic_from_bank_published_text` and set "
"`provisional_pending_specimen=True`, so this adapter itself flags their "
"corpus basis as provisional. No assigned file persists records or "
"declares freshness/reload policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:42
msgid "Security and safety"
msgstr "Seguridad y protección"

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:44
msgid ""
"The declaration and Modelo 100 byte entry points can keep decrypted PDF "
"bytes in memory, and source references are digest-derived rather than "
"exposing the input path in successful observations. The declaration "
"PDFium fast path is canary-guarded and closes PDF objects; its caches "
"retain extracted page text in process memory, up to 256 entries. The "
"mapped-tabular provider retains source rows in raw transaction fields, "
"including descriptions and counterparty values; persistence controls are "
"outside this chunk. The ledger exception translator places the full input"
" path and resolved provider error text in application error context "
"(financial/ledger_import.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/inbound/financial/ledger_import.py`)), so "
"downstream error presentation and logging should be checked for path "
"disclosure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:46
msgid ""
"For e-invoices, the parser treats external XML as hostile and blocks "
"entity/DTD handling through `defusedxml`, bounds XML bytes and nesting, "
"and uses `pikepdf` to validate PDF containers and read embedded files. "
"The attachment walk reads each embedded payload fully into memory before "
"the XML reader’s 32 MiB limit is applied, and the PDF container itself "
"has no local byte cap; very large PDF attachments are therefore a "
"conditional memory-exhaustion risk. No signature, issuer authentication, "
"or invoice authenticity verification appears in these assigned files. "
"Structured parsing avoids sending those documents through an LLM by "
"design, but correctness and authenticity still depend on the source and "
"later verification steps. No parser-specific authorization or redaction "
"layer is present in this chunk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:48
msgid "Implementation assessment"
msgstr "Evaluación de la implementación"

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:50
msgid ""
"The strongest implementation features are explicit unsupported behavior "
"for unobserved censo layouts, strict registry-profile extraction for "
"filed declarations, checksummed tax-ID validation in declaration parsing,"
" bounded hardened XML parsing, role-based seller/buyer mapping, and "
"honest provisional corpus metadata on mapped-tabular imports. Error types"
" carry structured extraction failures instead of requiring message "
"parsing. Source comments name fixtures and tests for parser behavior and "
"schema payload names, but the tests themselves are outside this chunk and"
" were not run or inspected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:52
msgid ""
"Confirmed local issues are the `parse_mode`/profile behavior mismatch for"
" borrador and the declaration snapshot check’s model-only compatibility "
"validation. The declaration success path also suppresses tolerated "
"missing-target information. Other risks depend on callers or external "
"code: the broad fallback IVA-ID heuristic is not checksum validation; "
"e-invoice DTO fields can be absent; profile quality and provisional "
"layout disclosure must be honored downstream; the column-role resolver "
"receives the full normalized table object and should be checked to "
"confirm it uses header vocabulary only; and provider detection/exception "
"presentation are implemented elsewhere. These are follow-up questions "
"rather than proven defects in the unseen layers. The assigned files "
"contain no runnable test suite or coverage output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:54
msgid "Dependencies and follow-up"
msgstr "Dependencias y seguimiento"

#: ../../technical/articles/002-inbound-document-and-financial-adapters.md:56
msgid ""
"Synthesis should trace the registry authority and profile definitions "
"that declaration parsing consumes, the downstream handling of tolerated "
"missing values and provisional profiles, the PDF text and redaction "
"helpers, the e-invoice application use and authenticity checks, the "
"`resolve_column_roles` boundary, and the financial provider detection and"
" transaction persistence flow. It should also check whether registry "
"snapshots passed into `parse_declaracion` are guaranteed elsewhere to "
"match the template year, revision, and period."
msgstr ""

